{"ts": "2026-10-16T16:49:14.526678Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T1648Z-22fc", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 7, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "H-e0757174", "decision": "reject", "by": "human", "reason": "Two spec violations in the production code, both reproduced by a reviewer; the gates passed because the tests stub these code paths. (1) init_telemetry() raises ModuleNotFoundError when the opentelemetry package is not installed: _sdk_available calls importlib.util.find_spec(\"opentelemetry.sdk\"), which raises when the parent package is missing (telemetry.py around 668-670, reached from _resolve_state and init_telemetry outside the try), so a plain install without the otel extra crashes the API at startup and breaks \"init SHALL NOT raise\". Fix: wrap find_spec in try/except (ImportError, ValueError) returning False; add a test that does NOT stub _sdk_available (monkeypatch importlib.util.find_spec to raise ModuleNotFoundError): auto returns False with no warning, true returns False with one WARNING that names mintmory-core[otel]. (2) _GuardedMetricExporter is never wired in: _build_meter_provider gives the raw exporter to PeriodicExportingMetricReader (telemetry.py around 453-465), so a ", "text_sha256": "05f8056b48da5aa5cc54ef364c92680c1d874328ebcb036e699149f7544ba281", "answer_sha256": "b4c4b07e7765860b546a5f1b084b3496ca668180f6ceeb5ba4efca0a7fb3d070"}
